*Always drop [[big bones]] which can be sold for guaranteed profit ({{Coins|{{GEP|Big bones}}}}) or used for [[Prayer]] experience while training.
* Faster aggression reset than Stronghold of Security, due to no doors. Just walk until you can't see giants on the minimap and return.
|disadvantages = * Highly crowded in most worlds.
*They can be a bit rough and tough against lower levels.
}}
{{Melee training monster
|name = [[Hobgoblin]]
|locations = [[Asgarnian Ice Dungeon]], [[Crandor]], [[Edgeville Dungeon]], west of [[Crafting Guild]]
|combat = 28, 42
|hitpoints = 29, 49
|requirements = [[Brass key]] (for the shed shortcut of [[Edgeville Dungeon]]), decent-to-mid-level combat
|recommendations = Your best armour ([[chainbody]] recommended) and weapons, and some moderate-to-high-healing food
|advantages = * A decent alternate monster of training your melee combat skills and profiting when hill giants are overcrowded.
*Level 42 hobgoblins have high HP of 49 but they are stronger than their level 28 counterparts and are recommended to be fought at 40+ melee levels.
*They have decent profitable drops for lower-level players as they very commonly drop [[limpwurt roots]] ({{Coins|{{GEP|Limpwurt root}}}}) and they have access to the [[gem drop table]] that rarely drop [[uncut gem]]s.
*They drop similar runes as hill giants do (except for [[death rune]]s) but they don't drop them as often as hill giants.
|disadvantages = * They can be a bit rough and tough against lower levels, especially the Level 42 hobgoblins.
}}

===Levels 40 to 60+===
{{Melee training monster
|name = [[Moss giant]]
|locations = [[Varrock Sewers]], [[Crandor]]
|combat = 42
|hitpoints = 60
|requirements = Mid-level combat, a [[knife]] or slash weapon if travelling in the Varrock Sewers to cut webs.
|recommendations = Food, armour ([[chainbody]] recommended), [[staff of fire]] and [[nature rune]]s for [[High Level Alchemy]], runes for [[Varrock Teleport]]
|advantages = *Fairly high HP for level.
*Decent alchable drops such as [[black sq shield]] ({{Coins|691}}), [[mithril sword]] ({{Coins|507}}), and [[steel kiteshield]] ({{Coins|510}}).
*Good rune drops such as [[law rune]]s, [[nature rune]]s, [[chaos rune]]s, [[cosmic rune]]s, and rarely [[death rune]]s.
*Chance of dropping a [[mossy key]], which allows the player to fight [[Bryophyta]], who also has good alchable drops. Additionally, Bryophyta can rarely drop its [[Bryophyta's essence|essence]] ({{Coins|{{GEP|Bryophyta's essence}}}}) which can be crafted into [[Bryophyta's staff]] ({{Coins|{{GEP|Bryophyta's staff (uncharged)}}}}) by bringing the essence and {{Coins|50,000}} to [[Zaff]] at his store in [[Varrock]].
*Always drops [[big bones]] which can be sold for guaranteed profit ({{Coins|{{GEP|Big bones}}}}) or used for [[Prayer]] experience while training.
*They have access to the [[gem drop table]] and rarely drop [[uncut gem]]s.
|disadvantages = *Varrock Sewers are often crowded.
*Hits hard if you have low Defence or weak armour.
*All of their (F2P) locations are far from a bank
}}

